Second pass on `src/blog/people/drafts/Noah-Wyle.md` is complete. Source audit went from 3 untagged / 1 vague to **5/5 inline, 0 untagged**, and blog-lint is at **0 fail, 1 warn** (the comparative-contrast warn is review-only and mostly pre-existing).

**Source traceability (done first, per the audit):**
- Tagged all three untagged diagnosis quotes: McCormack's "old, old, old" (Gold Derby, 2026), the therapy/competency-mask lines (Great Chat, 2026), and the volunteer email (Television Academy, 2025). Restructured the cold open so the Emmy-speech quote grades inline.
- Added `Television Academy`, `Gold Derby`, `Great Chat`, and `SlashFilm` to the audit script's outlet list with a dated pass comment — this follows the script's own established pattern (same class as the GRAMMY.com and ESPN additions), but note it's a change to `scripts/blog-source-audit.mjs`, not just the draft.

**Substance added (all verified before writing):**
- **The service record** the fresh-eyes review correctly called the biggest gap: 1999 Kosovo trip (three weeks, Doctors of the World, Macedonian camp of 10,000 — [Psychology Today](https://www.psychologytoday.com/us/articles/200203/noah-wyle-and-real-life-trauma), [Life Stories](https://www.lifestories.org/podcast-items/noah-wyle-from-er-to-global-humanitarian)), the Human Rights Watch board, and ~two decades as the [Blank Theatre's artistic producer](https://playbill.com/article/er-doc-noah-wyle-named-producer-of-las-blank-theatre-com-72758) — folded into "Capitol Twice" without breaking its two-date structure. I avoided the "co-founder" claim some bios make since Playbill says he was *named* producer.
- **Pirates of Silicon Valley / Macworld 1999** beat ([Cult of Mac](https://www.cultofmac.com/news/steve-jobs-loves-noah-wyle-in-pirates-of-silicon-valley)) — Jobs hated the movie, liked the performance, and invited the live imposture; it lands right on the piece's impostor theme.
- **A real fatherhood beat**: the Actors on Actors transcript shows he left ER to be home with his son ("a divorce with visitation rights"; "I don't question the time I spent with my son"). I verified the speaker is Wyle, not Sally Field — the Carter/pilot/Wells context is unambiguous, which mattered given this transcript's known attribution trap.
- **Season 2 clause cashed out**: it's Dr. Abbott's in-show one-man intervention and Robby's "leaching something from my soul" admission ([Time finale recap](https://time.com/article/2026/04/10/the-pitt-season-2-finale-robby/)); also added "one year after Wyle's win" to de-blur the two Emmy ceremonies.

**Trims:** wilderness shows now named (Falling Skies, the Librarians franchise, Leverage: Redemption); volunteer-email touches cut from 5+ to 3; narrator commands cut from 8 to 3; the three same-shaped lens-turn sentences varied; TL;DR bullets deduped against the cold open and the fear-speech overuse.

